        name = "Flameward Hippogryph",
        mountCategory = "Achievements",
        stepCount = 8,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - The quests are simple at high level, but Marks of the World Tree require weeks of daily resets.\n\n1. Enter the original Mount Hyjal campaign and quest through the regrowth storyline to Aessina's Miracle. Enable Trivial Quests. If NPCs vanish because you have an unfinished BfA Heart of Azeroth visit, finish the active A Fresh Trauma sequence before resuming Hyjal; do not start unrelated BfA prerequisites on a character without that phasing problem.\n\n2. At the Sanctuary of Malorne (about 27.1,62.5), take Guardians of Hyjal: Firelands Invasion! or the available Opening the Door follow-up. Complete the defense introduction and the offered sanctuary dailies. Save 20 Marks of the World Tree for Calling for Reinforcements, then follow the chain through the portal into the Molten Front.\n\n3. Complete the base dailies from Malfurion's Breach, then return to the Hyjal sanctuary for its daily quests as well. Keep both areas in your circuit; unlocking more quests increases your mark income. Save 150 Marks to recruit either the Shadow Wardens or the Druids of the Talon.\n\n4. After the first recruitment, finish that faction's daily route whenever available and save another 150 Marks to recruit the other group. Both are required. Once both are unlocked you choose which route to do that day, rather than completing both daily branches every day.\n\n5. After recruiting the Shadow Wardens, fight the ground-based Druids of the Flame in the Widow's Clutch near the solar core, around 70.4,38.4. These are the humanoid/shapeshifting druids, not the flying birds. Look for a Dried Acorn on the ground beside a killed druid. Pick up The Mysterious Seed, return it to Avrilla at Malfurion's Breach (50.4,87.0), then finish Planting Season and Little Lasher. The acorn is a ground object, not ordinary corpse loot.\n\n6. On a Druids of the Talon route, follow Into the Fire into the underground Molten Flow. Find the injured Anren Shadowseeker on rocks in the lava near 51.9,31.0, accept Need... Water... Badly... and escort him back to Thisalee Crow. This pin is underground: a surface quest marker does not mean he is standing above the cave. Finish the turn-in for Save Anren Shadowseeker.\n\n7. After both recruitment paths are unlocked, complete Calling the Ancients, Filling the Moonwell and Additional Armaments for 125 Marks each. Calling the Ancients first opens more daily income; follow each new quest marker and turn-in instead of stopping at the currency handover. All three projects are required.\n\n8. Open The Molten Front Offensive (5866) and check every criterion: sanctuary defense, entering the Front, both recruits, Little Lasher, Anren and the three projects. Finish any unchecked one on the character with that campaign progress. Check the Mount Journal for Flameward Hippogryph; if not learned automatically, also check Malfurion's reward mail.",
