        name = "Pureblood Fire Hawk",
        mountCategory = "Dungeon and Raids",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - A full raid route and a low drop chance can require many weekly attempts.\n\n1. Fly to Firelands in southern Mount Hyjal at 47.2,78.1. Choose legacy Normal or Heroic before entering. Both can drop the mount; Heroic is no longer a guaranteed egg.\n\n2. Clear the entrance trash and the Molten Fields until Shannox appears. Kill Shannox and his hounds. Defeat Beth'tilac to the northwest, Lord Rhyolith to the northeast and Alysrazor in the eastern arena. Alysrazor is also a separate chance at Flametalon.\n\n3. At Beth'tilac, kill a hanging Cinderweb Spinner and use its web strand to climb to the canopy. Damage Beth'tilac and follow the transition back down, then finish her. At Rhyolith, attack a foot until his armor breaks, then kill his exposed body.\n\n4. Defeat Baleroc at the northern gate after the initial bosses. Cross the bridge into Sulfuron Keep and kill Majordomo Fandral Staghelm. Continue to Ragnaros at the far end of the keep.\n\n5. Defeat Ragnaros and loot the encounter's reward. On Normal he submerges at the end; open the resulting Cache of the Fire Lord. On Heroic finish the additional final phase and loot the reward there. Look for Smoldering Egg of Millagazor, not an item named Pureblood Fire Hawk.\n\n6. Use the egg if it drops. Otherwise leave, change to the other difficulty and clear its independent weekly lockout. Once both Normal and Heroic are looted, use another character or wait for the weekly reset; switching 10/25 does not create four attempts.",
